Why We Are Ready to Proceed with Front-End Development
1. Full Business Logic Support with Procedures
We have designed targeted stored procedures that fully cover the application's main operations:

SubmitReport handles report submission, including location, category, priority, and description recording.
UpdateReportStatus manages report status updates, automatically awarding or deducting points and sending user notifications.
AwardPoints, SubmitRequest, PublishMunicipalityPost, HandleFalseReport, GetUserReportHistory, and SubmitFeedback procedures ensure clear workflows for citizen actions, municipal interactions, and feedback processing.
2. Real-Time Reactions with Database Triggers
We have set up critical database triggers to automate actions without relying on manual intervention:

After updating a report’s status (e.g., Completed, Rejected), users are notified and points are awarded or deducted accordingly.
After submitting a report, users receive instant confirmation.
After awarding points, the citizen’s total points are automatically recalculated.
After a municipality post is published, all users are notified.
After chatbot feedback is submitted, satisfaction statistics are updated if applicable.
3. Clear Table Structure Supporting All Use Cases
The database tables (e.g., cityzen, reports, points, municipality_post, ai_chat) are clearly structured and interconnected.
All user roles (citizen and municipality) and system features (report tracking, points rewards, chatbot communication, and statistics reporting) are fully supported through the existing schema.
4. Alignment with Project Requirements
The procedures and triggers directly reflect the use cases you defined:

Citizens can submit, track, and evaluate reports.
Municipalities can manage and resolve reports, communicate with citizens, and publish news.
An automated notification system keeps everyone informed at every important event.
5. Front-End Can Now Focus Purely on Interaction
Thanks to the strong backend foundation:

The front-end will simply call the existing procedures for each action (e.g., submit report, update status, redeem points).
Real-time updates (like notifications and points updates) are already handled by triggers, reducing complexity on the front-end side.

